From c19038822caa659b42600e7fb88d270b3d358526 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UmaJ56 <uma.jaganathan@qbiccatalyst.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 16:05:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Fix L2/L5 ticket visibility, notification 404, and L1
 resubmit persistence

- operatorTickets /tickets: scope supervisor visibility by the reports_to_user_id reporting chain (recursive), so an L2/L3/L4 sees every ticket owned by anyone below them regardless of status or whether approval_lN_user_ids was populated. Ensures reports_to_user_id column exists first.
- operatorTickets approval queue: scope by the logged-in approver so each level only sees its own tickets; persist resolved L2 approvers on resubmit.
- Header: rewrite broken /operator-tickets and /supervisor-tickets notification links (404) to the real /operatordetail and /supervisordetails routes by viewer level.
- SupervisorDashboard: keep L1 resubmitted ticket visible with Submit status instead of vanishing; let L5 and admin see every status under Mapped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 backend/routes/operatorTickets.routes.js      | 63 ++++++++++++++++++-
 frontend/src/components/Header.jsx            | 22 ++++++-
 .../src/views/tickets/SupervisorDashboard.js  | 13 +++-
 3 files changed, 94 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/backend/routes/operatorTickets.routes.js b/backend/routes/operatorTickets.routes.js
index 0e9d0d1c..8c9b9002 100644
